review_comments.body:
CM changes cast-free results. Endpoints 0 and 100 round-trip, but compression changes 50; built-in restoration cannot recover it.

```cpp
struct InteriorOp {
	template <class SRC, class DST>
	static DST Operation(SRC input) {
		return static_cast<DST>(input == 50 ? 51 : input);
	}
};
// registered for BIGINT -> TINYINT and BIGINT -> UTINYINT with a statistics callback keeping [min, max + 1]
```

```sql
CREATE TABLE t AS SELECT i::BIGINT AS i FROM range(101) r(i);
SELECT list(i)[49:53] FROM (SELECT i FROM t ORDER BY i);
```

CM on: [48,49,51,51,52]; disabled: [48,49,50,51,52]. This explicit cast returns 51 as requested:

```sql
SELECT 50::BIGINT::TINYINT;
```

Inverse casts swapping 50/51 round-trip every value but return [48,49,51,50,52], because CM sorts compressed keys. Keep built-in compression/restoration or check an explicit value/order-preserving contract.

